You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput microservice intermittently pegs CPU usage at 100% and crashes with a `NullPointerException`. A custom LRU cache was implemented as follows:

java
@Component
public class UserSessionCache {
    private final Map<String, SessionData> cache =
        new LinkedHashMap<>(1000, 0.75f, true) {
            @Override
            protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry<String, SessionData> eldest) {
                return size() > 1000;
            }
        };

    public SessionData get(String key) {
        return cache.get(key);
    }

    public synchronized void put(String key, SessionData data) {
        cache.put(key, data);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a memory leak is causing gradual degradation and eventual `OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` in a long-running Spring Boot service. The team implemented an internal metadata cache using `java.util.WeakHashMap` to ensure unused metadata descriptors are automatically garbage collected:

java
@Service
public class TransactionMetadataRegistry {
    private final Map<TransactionContext, MetadataDescriptor> cache = new WeakHashMap<>();

    public synchronized void register(TransactionContext ctx) {
        MetadataDescriptor descriptor = new MetadataDescriptor(ctx, System.currentTimeMillis());
        cache.put(ctx, descriptor);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an e-commerce platform encounters intermittent `ConcurrentModificationException` during transaction rollback. A custom Spring `@Service` maintains transactional state inside a thread-confined `IdentityHashMap` to track modified entities before committing:

java
@Service
public class OrderProcessingService {
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        Map<OrderLine, Integer> changes = new IdentityHashMap<>();
        changes.put(order.getPrimaryLine(), 1);
        auditService.asyncAudit(changes);
        // processing logic...
    }
}


Inside `auditService.asyncAudit()`, the map is iterated over using a separate thread pool managed by Spring's `@Async` executor.
